<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bronze Age</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze">Bronze</a> Age is the period in which bronze was the dominant material for tools and weapons, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> lasting from about the late fourth millennium to around 1200 BCE. Its late phase saw a system of great powers including the Egyptian Empire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni Empire</a>. It ended in the widespread collapse of the twelfth century BCE, after which Phoenician cities, ancestors of Punic civilisation, rose to prominence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bronze-age.jpg" alt="Bronze Age" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Want · CC BY-SA 3.0 cz · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Metallurgical_diffusion.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
